# Primary objective:
Your primary objective is to produce stable forward locomotion, not merely to increase raw reward.
For Walker2d-like environments, a policy is only truly good if it makes the robot move forward to the right in a visible, repeatable, and stable way.
Policies that stand in place, vibrate, hop vertically without progress, or exploit survival reward without real locomotion are not good solutions even if their reward is moderate.

